WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:01.470
METE ATAMEL: Video
intelligence API

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.740
can be used to do label
detection, explicit content

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.200
detection, and shot change
detection in videos.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.980
Let's see how to use the Video
Intelligence API with C#.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.830
First, make sure the API
is enabled in your project

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.500
and a service account
exists to make API calls.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.290
Both are explained in the
codelab in the video notes.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.550
In Cloud Shell, let's create a
simple .NET console app and add

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.080
Video Intelligence API NuGet
package to the project.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.980
We'll do label
detection in a video

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.870
stored on Google Cloud Storage.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:35.100
Open the online code editor
and navigate to Program.cs.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.770
Reference to the Video
Intelligence API library.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.690
Create Video
Intelligence client.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.370
Create a request pointing to
the video file in Cloud storage.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.050
Code annotate the video
with the request and wait

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.050
for the results.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.390
Finally, add some
code to print results.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.430
Let's run the app.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.270
There you go.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.240
You just extracted labels
from a video using the Video

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.300
Intelligence API.

